{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1377721-be-prepared","id":1377721,"title":"Be prepared!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-01T05:46:30-07:00","id":1377721,"title":"Be prepared!","content":"Hello everyone!<br /> <br /> I am still relatively new to the game of Mage and I am trying to learn the basics so to speak which is certainly easier said than done as there is so much to learn and absorb haha, I absolutely love it! On the tradition side I currently have a Dreamspeaker and a Hermetic mage, both of them with their own unique charms for sure. What I have learned however is that magic is extremely difficult, not to mention inefficient to throw &quot;on the fly&quot; so to speak and I have heard the recommendations from my ST that mages benefit a lot from being prepared and plan ahead when it comes to their magic.<br /> <br /> <br /> I am absolutely onboard with the concept as such, magic should be hard and difficult to cast as you are basically trying to reshape reality using our will and belief. The problem I have is that this is a lot easier said than done when you are on arete 2, especially so if you do not have any prime as you cannot really create any charms, nor can you &quot;hang&quot; any spells in preparation with time. So my question is this as &quot;simple&quot; as such, namely what you can do to make your magical &quot;punches&quot; more effective on the levels of arete 2 and 3 and what options that exist for those who do not play around with charms, talismans, fetishes and so on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25626-eiryth","name":"Eiryth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25626_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T07:15:54-07:00","id":1377727,"title":"","content":"In general one uses ritual magick to cast long lasting effects, that are also potent. Even at Arete 2 you should be able to get enough successes to get a decent Duration on low level spells. Esp. if you have a Cult, help from the other mages of the Chantry (requires compatible Focuses) and/or resources that lower the difficulty of your casting.<br /> <br /> Also being &quot;prepared&quot; has a lot to do with being informed. Low level magick and Knowledges are good to gain information of your enemies to prepare the kind of spells that you will need","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-01-2020, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}